# Pure Canvas — Design System Specification

> The institutional-grade visual language powering the ZaneAI mobile experience.

---

## 1. Philosophy

Pure Canvas is a **reduction-first** design system. Every element earns its place by proving it communicates information—not decoration. The system eliminates visual noise (shadows, fills, gradients, heavy borders) and replaces it with **structured emptiness**, **monochrome hierarchy**, and **typographic weight** as the primary tools of visual communication.

### Core Principles

| Principle | Rule |
|---|---|
| **No shadows** | Zero `elevation`, zero `shadowOpacity`. Period. |
| **Transparent containers** | Cards, groups, and option tiles use `backgroundColor: "transparent"` with a 1px `divider` border |
| **Typography is the UI** | `Manrope_800ExtraBold` carries visual weight—not color fills or background tints |
| **Monochrome selection** | Selected states use `textPrimary` (black/white), never the red accent, for borders and checkmarks |
| **Accent is surgical** | `#EC2D35` appears only on brand-critical touchpoints: CTA buttons, the brand dot, icon accents that signal "AI" or "settings" |
| **1px borders only** | All structural lines use `divider` color at 8% opacity. Selected states upgrade to 2px `textPrimary` |

---

## 2. Color System

### 2.1 Light Mode

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  background       #FFFFFF                       │
│  backgroundSoft   #FAFAFA                       │
│  surface          #F4F4F5                       │
│  surfaceRaised    #F4F4F5                       │
│  divider          rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08)           │
│  border           rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05)           │
│                                                 │
│  textPrimary      #000000                       │
│  textSecondary    #52525B                       │
│  textMuted        #A1A1AA                       │
│                                                 │
│  accent           #EC2D35                       │
│  success          #16A34A                       │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### 2.2 Dark Mode

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  background       #000000                       │
│  backgroundSoft   #0A0A0A                       │
│  surface          #121212                       │
│  surfaceRaised    #1A1A1A                       │
│  divider          rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08)     │
│  border           rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.10)     │
│                                                 │
│  textPrimary      #FFFFFF                       │
│  textSecondary    #A3A3A3                       │
│  textMuted        #737373                       │
│                                                 │
│  accent           #EC2D35                       │
│  success          #22C55E                       │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### 2.3 Color Roles

| Token | Purpose | Usage |
|---|---|---|
| `background` | Page/screen base | `Screen`, `ScrollView` backgrounds |
| `backgroundSoft` | Subtle depth layer | Reserved, rarely used in Pure Canvas |
| `surface` | **Legacy** — avoid in new components | Was used for card fills; now replaced by `"transparent"` |
| `surfaceRaised` | **Legacy** — avoid in new components | Was used for icon boxes; now replaced by transparent + border |
| `divider` | Structural separator | 1px borders on cards, icon boxes, group wrappers |
| `textPrimary` | Highest contrast text | Headlines, labels, selected-state borders and checkmarks |
| `textSecondary` | Supporting text | Descriptions, metadata |
| `textMuted` | Lowest priority text | Placeholders, captions, timestamps |
| `accent` | Brand red `#EC2D35` | **Surgical use only** — CTA buttons, brand dot, AI-related icons |
| `success` | Positive confirmation | Verification badges (used sparingly) |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> In the Pure Canvas system, `surface` and `surfaceRaised` are **not** used for new component backgrounds. All containers are `"transparent"` with `divider` borders. These tokens remain in the codebase for backward compatibility but should not appear in new UI.

---

## 3. Typography

### 3.1 Font Families

| Font | Weight | Token | Usage |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Manrope 500 Medium** | 500 | `Manrope_500Medium` | Body text, captions, base prose |
| **Manrope 600 SemiBold** | 600 | `Manrope_600SemiBold` | Subtitles, input text, labels |
| **Manrope 700 Bold** | 700 | `Manrope_700Bold` | Display headings (`variant="display"`) |
| **Manrope 800 ExtraBold** | 800 | `Manrope_800ExtraBold` | **Primary UI weight** — section headers, item labels, tab names, group eyebrows, option titles |

### 3.2 Arabic / RTL Typography

| Font | Weight | Token | Mapping |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Cairo 400 Regular** | 400 | `Cairo_400Regular` | Maps to `body` and `caption` |
| **Cairo 600 SemiBold** | 600 | `Cairo_600SemiBold` | Maps to `label` |
| **Cairo 700 Bold** | 700 | `Cairo_700Bold` | Maps to `display` and `title` |

The `<Text>` primitive auto-detects Arabic content using `isArabic()` and swaps the font family + sets `textAlign: "right"` and `writingDirection: "rtl"`.

### 3.3 Type Scale

| Variant | Size | Line Height | Default Font |
|---|---|---|---|
| `display` | 30px | 36px | Manrope 700 Bold |
| `title` | 20px | 26px | Manrope 600 SemiBold |
| `body` | 15px | 22px | Manrope 500 Medium |
| `label` | 13px | 18px | Manrope 600 SemiBold |
| `caption` | 12px | 16px | Manrope 500 Medium |

### 3.4 Override Convention

The type scale defines default weights. Pure Canvas **overrides** these inline with `Manrope_800ExtraBold` for interactive UI elements:

```tsx
// Section eyebrow
{ fontSize: 10, fontFamily: "Manrope_800ExtraBold", letterSpacing: 2, textTransform: "uppercase" }

// Menu item label
{ fontFamily: "Manrope_800ExtraBold" }

// Option card title
{ fontWeight: "800", fontFamily: "Manrope_800ExtraBold" }
```

